      "side": 1,
      "message": "What is the documented reason why people should follow this workflow?\n\nIs it like a linux kernel policy, do we have a link? Is it a new idea?\n\nPlease either provide a link or some reasoning.\n\nI believe this workflow is **worse in many cases**\n\n- increases maintainer workload due to solving trivial merge conflicts\n- increases timeline delay for rework.\n  If maintainers cannot solve nontrivial merge conflicts\n  quickly, they may have to ask a contributor to do work they could have\n  done earlier\n- authorship becomes less clear, does the maintainer always add their signoff?\n  If not, where is the line, solving a nontrivial conflict could\n  *significantly* change the patch.\n- increases timeline delay due to maintainers needing to wait for CI to pass\n  before submitting on patches they rebased themselves\n\n\nOverall i agree there should not be random changes done to a patch without feedback\n(potentially resetting review progress / not converging)\nbut this reads different.",
